{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter and Online Dating"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Finding Your Other Half"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le11ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking about Wishes and Imaginary Situations  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">\u201cI wish ... \u201d</span> to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> introduces an idea. After <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense. <br/><br/> I wish I knew ... <br/> I wish I had ... <br/> I wish you were ... <br/> I wish I was/were ... <br/><br/>  Structure: <br/> Wish + Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish I were as successful with girls as you are. <br/><br/> I wish I was less awkward.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I want to be as successful as you, but I'm not.<br/><br/>  I want to be less awkward but I can't.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish she liked me.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She probably doesn't like me.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is possible to use either <span class=\"strong\">was</span> or <span class=\"strong\">were</span> in the structure.  <span class=\"strong\">Were</span> is the more grammatically correct way to form the sentence, but <span class=\"strong\">was</span> is common in conversation. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modal Verbs for Speculating"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> may</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> might</span>, and could to describe degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>  Must = it's very likely <br/> Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br/> May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br/> May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true <br> <br> You can use them in the present or perfect tenses. When you use them in the perfect tense, you are speculating about the past. <br> For example:  <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">may have been</span> busy when you tried to call. </span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That must feel natural for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's very likely it's natural for you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It can't be hard for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's not possible that it's hard for you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I could've fallen for her.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible I would have fallen for her.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That may not have been easy for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible it wasn't easy for you.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "*Remember that in conversation, using the contracted form of the verb phrase is common (could have = could've)."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to match up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be well together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The date was great. I thought we matched up pretty well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about dating."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lead on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to let someone believe things that may not be true"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I realized that she was leading me on, so we broke up."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hit it off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get along well immediately"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We hit it off immediately and had a lot of fun on our first date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall for "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to have strong romantic feelings towards somebody"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I could have fallen for her, but I realized that she was leading me on."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le11ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "head over heels"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "madly in love"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"